Hooks see the resolved `--target`, not the declared `artifact:`: a `frontmatter-update` without a
file target writes the target file, and a script hook receives it in `BOOPING_ARTIFACT`.

-- fixtures/home/Claude/_playbooks/fx-hooks/playbook.md --
---
name: fx-hooks
title: Hooks
summary: Hook-bearing fixture for playbook-transition.
---

Preamble.
-- fixtures/home/Claude/_playbooks/fx-hooks/playbook.yaml --
state: main
graph:
  only: []

states:
  main:
    artifact: index.md
    initial: intaking
    statuses:
      intaking:
        transitions:
          - to: noted
            when: the environment is recorded
            hooks: ["frontmatter-update researched=yes", "script env-note"]
      noted: {terminal: true}
-- fixtures/home/Claude/_playbooks/fx-hooks/only/prompt.md --
---
summary: Only step.
---

Only body.
-- fixtures/home/Claude/_playbooks/fx-hooks/_scripts/env-note --
#!/bin/sh
echo "artifact=$BOOPING_ARTIFACT" > "$BOOPING_WORKDIR/env.txt"
-- fixtures/cwd/run/review.md --
---
status: intaking
---
-- cmd --
chmod +x ../home/Claude/_playbooks/fx-hooks/_scripts/env-note
booping playbook-transition fx-hooks noted --target review.md --workdir run
-- exit --
0
